SOURCE-INSPECTION CAUTIONS
- A source construct is not an observed failure until a relevant test
  actually triggers the wrong behavior.
- Bug #9 includes reporter reproduction claims at a pinned commit;
  no local execution of its testcase was performed by this audit.
- The source uses hard-coded limits and a tutorial environment.
  A limit is a defect only when input constraints allow crossing it.
- A report about multi-producer safety does not prove a queue promised
  multi-producer support; first inspect intended ownership.
- The source socket loop uses AF_INET+AI_NUMERICHOST; do not assume more
  than one address candidate without checking the actual result set.
- This document has ZERO coding solutions.
